# =============================================================================
# Networthy API request catalog
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exercise a running Networthy from your IDE (VS Code "REST Client", JetBrains
# HTTP Client, etc.). Start it first — see RUNBOOK.md §2:
#   dotnet run --project src/Networthy.AppHost   (Aspire; take the networthy-api
#                                                 URL from the dashboard)
#   docker compose up -d                         (compose → http://localhost:8080)
#   RUNBOOK §2 Mode B                            (headless → http://127.0.0.1:8094)
#
# Auth: in Development the API accepts dev-auth headers (X-Dev-*) that stand in
# for a real OIDC token (RUNBOOK §3). system_admin holds *; Networthy's own
# roles are household-admin and household-member — send a narrower role to
# prove an RBAC 403. In production the headers are ignored.
#
# GUID/id placeholders are zeroed — copy real ids from the list responses above
# each request. When you add an endpoint, add its request here in the same PR.
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@subject = dev-user
@tenant = dev
@roles = system_admin

# Placeholders — replace with real ids from list responses.
@accountId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@transactionId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@budgetId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@goalId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@incomeSourceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@categoryId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@batchId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@approvalId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@fileId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ── Health (anonymous) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Liveness (never calls the LLM — safe to poll)
GET {{baseUrl}}/alive

### Readiness / health checks (DB, Redis reachable)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

# ── Platform: identity + navigation ──────────────────────────────────────────

### Who am I — user, tenant, effective permissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/me
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Modules + tabs the caller can see (must contain "finance" — RUNBOOK §2 ready signal)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/modules
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Deployment facts (chat enabled? mock mode?)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/info
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Branding (name, colors the UI shell renders)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/branding
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### AI-decision disclosures (risk tier + what the AI may decide)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/ai-decisions
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

# ── Chat: a streamed agent turn (AG-UI over SSE) ─────────────────────────────

### One turn against the finance agent. The Mock provider routes by name-token
### match (RUNBOOK §4) and performs a real, audited tool call.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agui/finance
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{
  "messages": [{ "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "List our accounts" }]
}

### A gated write: fires CUSTOM(approval_required), executes NOTHING until approved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agui/finance
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{
  "messages": [{ "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Create a checking account called Catalog Demo" }]
}

# ── Chat: human-in-the-loop approvals ────────────────────────────────────────

### Pending approvals (side-effecting tool calls parked awaiting a human)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/approvals
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Approve — re-executes the exact recorded call; result is the tool's own return value
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/approvals/{{approvalId}}/approve
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Reject — discards the call; the executor is never invoked
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/approvals/{{approvalId}}/reject
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

# ── Notifications (self-scoped) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### My notification inbox
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### The preference switchboard (finance.bill, finance.budgets, finance.recurring,
### finance.statements, finance.imports, finance.approvals — on by default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/preferences
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Mute one category for MYSELF (per-user, never tenant-wide)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/preferences/finance.bill
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "enabled": false }

# ── Admin: security, audit, usage, ops ───────────────────────────────────────

### Every tool + the permission gating it. After adding a tool this MUST list it,
### or the manifest and FinanceToolSource disagree (RUNBOOK §4).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/security/catalog
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Roles and the permissions each grants
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Users in the household, with roles and active state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Tool-call audit (append-only; blocked calls carry "Blocked: tool requires human
### approval" — filter success==true && error==null for real executions, RUNBOOK §4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/audit/tool-calls
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Token usage (populated only after at least one chat turn)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/usage?days=30
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Ops snapshot — jobs, connectors, notifications, AI budget at a glance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ops
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Admin-console extension pages (finance ships exchange-rates + document-scanning)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/extensions
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

# ── Admin: AI settings (per-household provider; key is write-only) ───────────

### Current provider connection + prompts + budgets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ai-settings
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Models the selected provider offers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ai-models
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Switch provider at runtime (apiKey: null=keep stored, ""=clear, value=replace)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ai-settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "systemPrompt": null, "maxConversationTokens": null, "maxMonthlyTokens": null, "provider": "Mock", "model": "demo-model", "endpoint": null, "apiKey": null }

# ── Admin: OCR connectors (scanned-statement engines, default-off) ───────────

### Installed connectors + this household's enablement/settings (secrets report
### hasValue, never the value)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/connectors
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Point self-hosted OCR at a Tika server (Aspire parks one on :9998 — RUNBOOK §2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/connectors/ocr-apache-tika/settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "values": { "BaseUrl": "http://localhost:9998" } }

### Enable it (order matters: settings first, then enable)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/connectors/ocr-apache-tika/enable
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Disable (tools off immediately)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/connectors/ocr-apache-tika/disable
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Azure Document Intelligence is connector id ocr-azure-document-intelligence —
### its Endpoint/ApiKey setting keys are listed in the connectors catalog above.

# ── Finance: accounts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### List accounts (visibility-scoped; private accounts hidden from other members)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/accounts
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Create an account (types: checking | savings | credit | cash | loan;
### currencyCode blank = household default)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "name": "Chase Checking", "type": "checking", "currencyCode": "USD", "cachedBalance": 2500, "institutionName": "Chase" }

### Create a loan (APR + minimum payment power the debt-cost math)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "name": "House mortgage", "type": "loan", "cachedBalance": -250000, "interestRateApr": 6.25, "minimumMonthlyPayment": 1800, "institutionName": "Wells Fargo" }

### Delete an account
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/accounts/{{accountId}}
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

# ── Finance: transactions + transfers ────────────────────────────────────────

### List transactions (source column tags assistant/manual/upload rows;
### transferWith names a linked leg's counterpart account)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/transactions
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Add one (direction: expense | income; occurredOn optional = today)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "accountName": "Chase Checking", "description": "Groceries", "amount": 82.15, "direction": "expense", "categoryName": "Groceries" }

### Delete one
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/transactions/{{transactionId}}
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Link every HIGH-confidence detected transfer pair (the click IS the approval;
### linked legs stop counting as income/spending, balances unchanged)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/transfers/link-detected
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

